extends ./layout/layout-default
block content
  article.TextPage
    p.Eyebrow BEFORE YOUR FIRST SHIFT
    h1 How to play
    ol.PlaySteps
      li Shortlist 3 people in the first round, 5 in the next, and 8 in the last. A round ends when you reach its target, run out of CVs, or run out of time.
      li Start with six available CVs. The next rounds have ten and fourteen. Choose a person in the office or use Previous and Next to open a CV.
      li Read their skill, experience, academy, and city.
      li Choose Shortlist or Pass. You can also press S or P. Arrow keys switch CVs. Take your time in round one. You get 45 seconds in each later round. Missing a target does not block the story.
      li Check your saved choices, then train Scout using only those choices. Unreviewed CVs are excluded.
      li Watch Scout screen new CVs. Use Screen next CV to watch each choice, or Screen the rest to see the results straight away.
      li Add the company records and try Scout on the same CVs again. Compare the actual choices before and after.
      li Read your shift notes. Matching old hiring choices is different from matching a job check.
      li Look closer. Open two different independent CV checks. Each costs 1 of your 8 credits. Reopening a check is free. Follow each CV through Scout's actual questions.
      li Read the audit of 80 new CVs. Compare the overall result and the ready people shortlisted in each city.
      li In the workshop, try hiding an input, adding old records, or changing the training labels. The buttons show the cost. Undo refunds workshop purchases. The strictness control is free.
      li Choose Use this Scout when you are ready. Your setup locks before the final 200 CVs. You can watch 12 scans or skip the animation; the same 200 applicants are checked either way.
      li Read your audit receipt, add optional notes, and download or print it. A new shift starts with fresh data. Reloading lets you continue a saved shift.
    h2 The three final checks
    p Earn one star for matching at least 85% of job checks, one for shortlisting at least 75% of ready people in each city, and one for keeping the gap between those two city rates within 15 percentage points.
    p Use Pause or press Esc to take a break. Switching tabs also pauses the game. Sound is optional. You can play on a laptop, tablet or phone.
    h2 What will you notice?
    p Learning from past choices can copy the patterns in those choices. A fast answer is still worth checking.
    p Think about this as you play: does a past hiring choice tell us who can do the job?
    a.MainButton(href='./game/') Start your shift →
